{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "4735a962-821c-42f2-8484-dfaaaa6270c3",
		"name": "Easy connector API document",
		"description": "Requests for the easyCredit connector API, version 1.1.0, with pay by invoice (BILL_PAYMENT) and pay by installments (INSTALLMENT_PAYMENT). Run the folders in this order: 1 CommerceTools, 2 Payment, 3 Webhook. For create and authorize, run one of the two variants. A run stops after the create request, because the manual step on the easyCredit page follows. Then continue with 2.6. In the Collection Runner, deselect the other variant, and deselect 3.1 when you run 2.7 to 2.10. Before you start, set the environment variables. Set connector_url to the processor URL. After the deployment, the Connect deployment shows the URL of each application, and the processor URL is the URL of the application \"processor\". The processor also stores its own URL in the custom object with the container \"easycredit-connector\" and the key \"easycredit-connector-url\". Create a cart with a line item, a German billing address, a German shipping address and an amount inside the limits of the payment type. Use your usual commercetools tooling for this. Then put the cart ID in cart_id. See docs/ in the repository for each endpoint.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "39108604"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "1. CommerceTools",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "1.1 Obtain access token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"tests[\"Status code is 200\"] = responseCode.code === 200;",
									"var data = JSON.parse(responseBody);",
									"if(data.access_token){",
									"    pm.environment.set(\"ctp_access_token\", data.access_token);",
									"}",
									"if (data.scope) {",
									"    parts = data.scope.split(\" \");",
									"    parts = parts.filter(scope => scope.includes(\":\")).map(scope => scope.split(\":\"))",
									"    if (parts.length > 0) {",
									"        scopeParts = parts[0];",
									"        pm.environment.set(\"project-key\", scopeParts[1]);",
									"    }",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"packages": {}
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"auth": {
							"type": "basic",
							"basic": [
								{
									"key": "password",
									"value": "{{client_secret}}",
									"type": "string"
								},
								{
									"key": "username",
									"value": "{{client_id}}",
									"type": "string"
								}
							]
						},
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{auth_url}}/oauth/token?grant_type=client_credentials",
							"host": [
								"{{auth_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"oauth",
								"token"
							],
							"query": [
								{
									"key": "grant_type",
									"value": "client_credentials"
								}
							]
						},
						"description": "Gets a commercetools access token with the client credentials from the environment. The API client needs the scope manage_sessions for request 1.2. It needs one of the scopes manage_payments, manage_checkout_payment_intents or manage_project for Capture Payment and Refund Payment. Authorize needs only an active token. See docs/CommercetoolsFrontendIntegration.md#bff-api-client. The test script sets project-key from the scope of the token. It overwrites the value in the environment."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "1.2 Obtain Session ID",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"var data = JSON.parse(responseBody);",
									"if(data.id){",
									"    pm.environment.set(\"ctp_session_id\", data.id);",
									"}"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"packages": {}
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Authorization",
								"value": "Bearer {{ctp_access_token}}"
							},
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json",
								"type": "text"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n    \"cart\": {\n        \"cartRef\": {\n          \"id\": \"{{cart_id}}\"\n        }\n    },\n    \"metadata\": {\n        \"applicationKey\": \"{{checkout_application_key}}\"\n    }\n}",
							"options": {
								"raw": {
									"language": "json"
								}
							}
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{session_url}}/{{project-key}}/sessions",
							"host": [
								"{{session_url}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"{{project-key}}",
								"sessions"
							]
						},
						"description": "Creates a commercetools checkout session for the cart in cart_id, and saves it as ctp_session_id. The body uses the key of your Checkout application from checkout_application_key. The token needs the scope manage_sessions. See docs/CommercetoolsFrontendIntegration.md#checkout-session."
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "Run first. Run request 1.1 and then request 1.2. Request 1.1 saves the access token. Request 1.2 saves the session ID."
		},
